      "reasoning_content": "I need to write tests for UDNEmbedIE._real_extract. The class needs _VALID_URL for _match_id. The real UDN extractor has:\n\n```python\n_VALID_URL = r'https?://video\\.udn\\.com/(?:embed|play)/news/(?P<id>\\d+)'\n```\n\nI'll define the class in the test with the same code, or import from youtube_dl.extractor.udn. Better to import the real class: `from youtube_dl.extractor.udn import UDNEmbedIE`. But the code snippet given is the source; the test should exercise the real module. I'll import it.\n\nPlan tests, mocking _download_webpage and _extract_m3u8_formats/_extract_f4m_formats via monkeypatch on the instance or class.\n\nTest 1: options JSON parse path with youtube URL \u2192 url_result. Page contains `var options = {...};` with 'youtube' key. js_to_json converts single quotes. E.g.:\n\n```\nvar options = {\n  'video': {'youtube': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BspDutaDdBo'},\n  'title': 'test title',\n  'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'\n};\n```\n\njs_to_json handles single quotes \u2192 valid JSON. _parse_json parses. options truthy \u2192 video_urls = options['video'], title, poster. youtube truthy \u2192 return url_result. Assert result == {'_type': 'url', 'url': ..., 'ie_key': 'Youtube'}.\n\nTest 2: fallback path (options empty \u2014 e.g. `var options = {};`? Wait, if options is `{}` then `options or {}` \u2192 {} \u2192 falsy \u2192 else branch. But then trans_options_str must contain `\"video\"\\s*:\\s*({.+?})\\s*,` \u2014 regex on trans_options_str. Hmm, if options_str is `{}` then trans is `{}` and the regex `\"video\"\\s*:\\s*({.+?})\\s*,` won't match. Actually the else branch happens when _parse_json fails (fatal=False) \u2014 e.g. options_str is JS that js_to_json can't fully convert, or parse fails. E.g. `var options = {'video': {'mp4': '...'}, title: 'x'}` \u2014 unquoted key `title:` \u2014 js_to_json converts bare identifiers to quoted strings actually. js_to_json quotes identifiers too: `(?:(?<![0-9])[eE]|[